Both libraries are loaded via [38;5;10mlibloading[0m and compared by raw f32 bit pattern, so NaN payloads and the sign of zero are asserted. The [38;5;10mout[0m struct is pre-filled with a sentinel before every call, which is how the [38;5;10mc2RaytoCapsule[0m fall-through was caught writing [38;5;10mout->n[0m/[38;5;10mout->t[0m before returning 0. Nine rows additionally pin the C's sentinel with a hard [38;5;10massert_eq![0m (e.g. [38;5;10mc2AABBtoAABB[0m returns [1m1[22m on all-NaN input; [38;5;10mc2Absv(-0.0)[0m keeps the sign bit) so the tests fail loudly rather than silently agreeing with a wrong Rust.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Two caveats worth stating plainly. Null [38;5;10mout[0m and null [38;5;10mB[0m are dereferenced unconditionally by the C, so they are identical UB on both sides and are documented rather than tested — I verified this by inspection only. And the NaN-payload fidelity above is specific to x86-64 SSE semantics, which is what the C reference build targets; on another architecture the reference itself would behave differently.[0m[0m
